{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven","id":855762,"title":"Dark Era: The Wolf and the Raven","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-30T10:06:46-07:00","id":855762,"title":"Dark Era: The Wolf and the Raven","content":"We have a thread for the Neolithic Forsaken period so I thought it appropriate to open another one up for the Viking Werewolf era, shared with Sin-Eaters.<br /> <br /> What do you backers and non-backers who've heard of it or seen friends copies think? Any criticisms, compliments or comments?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T12:49:33-07:00","id":855903,"title":"","content":"It's definitely the densest chapter in the book; while the others settle for the movie version of history, this one goes hard on the actual Viking info.<br /> <br /> Some of the art is impressively bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T13:10:44-07:00","id":855924,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, for a chapter I expected so little from, I was genuinely impressed with how interesting and dynamic a setting it is for the Uratha. I have some gripes with how the Sin-Eaters don't feel fully integrated (Though I still love it to bits), but on the whole, this setting is rich and evocative-it's awesome to see the Uratha in another heyday setting that's quite different from their heyday in Sumer. I never cared much for the Meninna before, but the idea of doing one who has a raid come back to haunt them appeals to me quite a lot.<br /> <br /> And oh my god, Hearthglass Beads are the sweetest thing ever, you guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:46:18-07:00","id":856025,"title":"","content":"I'm glad they updated the Gift of Technology because I needed that for a game set during the Crusades that I might be playing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T17:02:06-07:00","id":856084,"title":"","content":"Hi! I wrote from Raiding &amp; Trading through to the Fire-Touched Lodge and a couple of the blurbs on other lines. I'm happy to answer questions if you have them. Apologies if &quot;dense&quot; was a bad thing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10426-m-murray","name":"M.Murray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T17:15:49-07:00","id":856092,"title":"","content":"As I said previously, I actually expected to get bored by that chapter. Instead, I was immensely entertained and excited for the setting. Good job to you and your fellows, again. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T17:15:50-07:00","id":856093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M.Murray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=856084#post856084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi! I wrote from Raiding &amp; Trading through to the Fire-Touched Lodge and a couple of the blurbs on other lines. I'm happy to answer questions if you have them. Apologies if &amp;quot;dense&amp;quot; was a bad thing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Dense is so not a problem; I'm perfectly happy with lots of history in my historical settings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T22:12:28-07:00","id":856956,"title":"","content":"( I\u2019m just before reading Auspices section )<br /> <br /> I have a bit mixed feelings about Viking chapter, but in the end positive, I think. I very like there are much historical accuracy even I did not know about or terms not known by me<br /> <br /> My biggest concern is downgraded role of religion in chapter - Norse gods got only one paragraph ( till moment I\u2019m in ) and Christianity is shown just as political force. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Integration of Old Gods with Uratha knowledge of Shadow is big issue, that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=426473#post426473\">we tried on ourselves to touch before chapter come out </a>and it is a bit mess- especially between worship of Firstborns and Norse Gods - I really hoped for more on this matter in Era chapter, really. <br /> Also, position of Church as more than political faction uniting Europe. In cWoD <b>Werewolf: Dark Ages</b>, the Church is Wyrm puppet, infiltrated by it and pervasive fighting with Northern Gaouru. In <i>Wolf and Raven</i> we have vampire here and there and maybe Claimed. Even shout out to mages Seers of Throne would make much bigger threat midst the Church. Not too mention that Christian temples could put interesting Bans on pagan werewolves from desecration of their holy sites.<br /> <br /> Other thing that bothers me is portraying of Uratha as \u201cjust explorers\u201d. \u201cViking werewolves comes to new land were are other werewolves, but working under the same packs\u201d - whole chapter read sounds like Uratha, on themselves, do not different wherever they are, they just on two sides of humans political conflict. I wanted some highlighting in difference between European wolves and North ones. Did not get it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> However, I very like hiding pack Totem in boats ornaments - it does have sens that Uratha would sail under banner of Totem, and we all know that boats have great animal decorations. This idea is really great! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For now, I\u2019m a bit disappointment on Viking Uratha culture parts itself. Historical - it\u2019s really good written. But I need a bit more how <i>werewolves </i>where different in those times. Or how Uratha seen their raids and wars targets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T23:37:01-07:00","id":856978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=856956#post856956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest concern is downgraded role of religion in chapter - Norse gods got only one paragraph ( till moment I\u2019m in ) and Christianity is shown just as political force. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Integration of Old Gods with Uratha knowledge of Shadow is big issue, that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=426473#post426473\">we tried on ourselves to touch before chapter come out </a>and it is a bit mess- especially between worship of Firstborns and Norse Gods - I really hoped for more on this matter in Era chapter, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>We tried it before - and it ended in arguments.<br /> <br /> Leaving it vague is MUCH better. That allows each troupe to play as they want without getting told by the book they are doing it wrong.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T01:15:15-07:00","id":857015,"title":"","content":"Reading futher - the Auspies and Tribes sections solves most of my Old Gods interpretiotion problems. Still Christianity seems to be &quot;whithout flavor&quot;...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T01:17:18-07:00","id":857017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857015#post857015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading futher - the Auspies and Tribes sections solves most of my Old Gods interpretiotion problems. Still Christianity seems to be &quot;whithout flavor&quot;...</div> </div> </div> </div>So... What would you have wanted?<br /> <br /> I'm fairly certain everyone here has at least an inkling about how Christianity works, and how to think of it. Focusing on it would be wasted word count, in many ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T05:28:36-07:00","id":857071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857017#post857017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So... What would you have wanted?<br /> <br /> I'm fairly certain everyone here has at least an inkling about how Christianity works, and how to think of it. Focusing on it would be wasted word count, in many ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I have to agree. I'm glad word count wasn't 'wasted' on stuff most already know.<br /> <br /> I probably jumped the gun with the thread, when I made it I had only skimmed the section and I only just read it last night. It's nicely organized, and we get an actual Hunting Ground and sections about the tribes and auspices, all very well done. There's also the mechanics section, which was sweet. The Lodge of Muspell was really interesting, and I honestly feel like I'm going to try and pick up that rite in my modern day because it looks incredibly useful, and fitting for our pack.<br /> <br /> All in all I really like it, but I feel like in some parts it could have been more ambitious, offering more werewolf-related story seeds than moments of human history you could insert your werewolves. But I'm being unfairly critical here, it's very well done and it makes a point of keeping the Uratha involved throughout the whole thing.<br /> <br /> I particularly liked the Restless Dead section, and the ambiguity of the things they come across and how they're formed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T16:48:50-07:00","id":857340,"title":"","content":"I tried to touch on how Norse Christianity differed in that their usual political processes didn't always work out. The Norse initially warmed to the concept of Christ a lot faster than they did to monotheism (as mentioned in the chapter). I did consider covering Christianity a bit more, but there were a couple of issues. As Seidmadr and nofather said, it seemed to be covering a lot of stuff people would know, which was non-specific to the region, and it was killing the word count. I actually had to cut a lot out and my section is still slightly over the assigned count. And nofather actually touched on another aspect of it that featured in the Restless Dead; I was going for ambiguity, and I like the idea that one supernatural species wouldn't have a whole lot of info on the others. I was a tad conscious of bashing the Christians a bit too much, and while oWoD has big nasty forces controlling the Church, 1st Ed and CofD always struck me as more reserved about that sort of thing, where the simple non-supernatural explanation was more likely than a large prevailing presence of one big bad. Consider also that the putting too many big nasty evil things behind the Church gives Vikings a nice moral motivation to hide behind that simply doesn't exist in real life, and that doesn't seem in keeping with the setting.<br /> <br /> It's worth pointing out, because it's a small reference, but Sitric was raiding the monasteries sponsored by other Christian leaders. It wasn't uncommon for Christian Vikings to find new excuses to keep raiding.<br /> <br /> I probably could've put some more story seeds in with the other stuff. Doing justice to that battle without over-simplifying it was challenging in the space I had. The St Bryce's Day Massacre and the ensuing conflict probably would've taken up a lot more space if I'd been expanding on that, but it was a less consolidated event and had less pay-off for players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10426-m-murray","name":"M.Murray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T00:58:38-07:00","id":857567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857017#post857017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... What would you have wanted?<br /> <br /> I'm fairly certain everyone here has at least an inkling about how Christianity works, and how to think of it. Focusing on it would be wasted word count, in many ways.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>We</i> know how Christianity works - the Norseman didn't. We also know how Christianity works NOW, not in early Middle Ages. <b>Mainly, I was looking for some nice Christianity related Werewolf story seeds - like how it works with spirits?</b> How Shadow answer to coming of new religion? What does Christian converted werewolf looks like in those times? HOW Christian packs in Europe differce from those in Vikings? I cannot show deep contrast on those with having only answer of one side of it.<br /> <br /> I was hoping a bit less stress was put on historical battles and more on showing this kind of thing. Battles I can easily find online - relation to fictional RPG epheremal beings between 1000 years before version of Christianity - not so much.<br /> <br /> Maybe I did not read to it, but I do not see any Bale Hounds shout out that should be <i>natural</i> in Christian dominated Europe. Old World should be <i>crawling</i> with Malejin worshiping Uratha when confronted with Christianity and it's view on","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T01:13:18-07:00","id":857576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M.Murray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857340#post857340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tried to touch on how Norse Christianity differed in that their usual political processes didn't always work out. The Norse initially warmed to the concept of Christ a lot faster than they did to monotheism (as mentioned in the chapter). I did consider covering Christianity a bit more, but there were a couple of issues. As Seidmadr and nofather said, it seemed to be covering a lot of stuff people would know, which was non-specific to the region, and it was killing the word count. I actually had to cut a lot out and my section is still slightly over the assigned count.</div> </div> </div> </div>In understand word count limitation - still, I would much rather read about setting related differences than list of all historical battles. It made me a bit disappointed in here - Viking cultural related stuff was really superb and introduced me to some concept I wasn't aware worth. But using few pages on most known battles could be used on showing more &quot;culture shock&quot; werewolves get by meetings on both sides.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M.Murray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857340#post857340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And nofather actually touched on another aspect of it that featured in the Restless Dead; I was going for ambiguity, and I like the idea that one supernatural species wouldn't have a whole lot of info on the others. I was a tad conscious of bashing the Christians a bit too much, and while oWoD has big nasty forces controlling the Church, 1st Ed and CofD always struck me as more reserved about that sort of thing, where the simple non-supernatural explanation was more likely than a large prevailing presence of one big bad. Consider also that the putting too many big nasty evil things behind the Church gives Vikings a nice moral motivation to hide behind that simply doesn't exist in real life, and that doesn't seem in keeping with the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not want to choose one enemy amidst Church - I want to <i>deepen</i> mystery of fighting with other religion. <br /> <br /> In chapter, sacking monasteries and chapels do not seem much different than attacking the towns or castles - so it's &quot;favourless&quot;. Mention here and there vampires or Claimed seems more like random encounters than fighting alien religion temple. I was hoping for maybe at weird Bans or curses going on raiders? &quot;Alien&quot; christian spirts, not found in Scandinavia? Maybe not even some detailed stats, just mentioning that Christianity <i>was</i> a problem for Norse werewolves, as ALIEN religion itself, even when human Vikings embraced it easily? That Uratha in Europe had some weird fetishes and Gifts? Some things like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M.Murray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857340#post857340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth pointing out, because it's a small reference, but Sitric was raiding the monasteries sponsored by other Christian leaders. It wasn't uncommon for Christian Vikings to find new excuses to keep raiding.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Great news - now how this relates to Uratha?</b> What does it gives me, as ST, to say to Viking Uratha and build story on this? 'You can attack your brothers in Christianity'? Well, what does this bring to my table?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M.Murray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857340#post857340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I probably could've put some more story seeds in with the other stuff. Doing justice to that battle without over-simplifying it was challenging in the space I had. The St Bryce's Day Massacre and the ensuing conflict probably would've taken up a lot more space if I'd been expanding on that, but it was a less consolidated event and had less pay-off for players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/857534-dark-eras-battle-mass-combat-rules\">Mass Combat Rules</a> in <b>Dark Eras</b> using battles itself as story scenario is dubious goal in first place.<br /> <br /> Maybe I didn't get to those ( I'm in Tribes part ) but I feel the chapter lacks story seeds and setting backgrounds where it should have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-02-2016, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T04:50:02-07:00","id":857623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857567#post857567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>We</i> know how Christianity works - the Norseman didn't. We also know how Christianity works NOW, not in early Middle Ages. <b>Mainly, I was looking for some nice Christianity related Werewolf story seeds - like how it works with spirits?</b> How Shadow answer to coming of new religion? What does Christian converted werewolf looks like in those times? HOW Christian packs in Europe differce from those in Vikings? I cannot show deep contrast on those with having only answer of one side of it.<br /> <br /> Medieval Christianity would be interesting, but of all the things to focus on, I'd say it is of less import than a religion that's actually dead. (Yes, there are revivals of the Old Faith, but we don't know everything, and it has been changed to fit modern ideas).</div> </div> </div> </div>But, what do you mean &quot;How Shadow answer to coming of new religion?&quot;?. It's not like the Shadow of today is particularly shaped by religion, except around important religious centres. And even then it is THAT things are being believed in that causes a stir, not WHAT is being believed in.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857567#post857567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was hoping a bit less stress was put on historical battles and more on showing this kind of thing. Battles I can easily find online - relation to fictional RPG epheremal beings between 1000 years before version of Christianity - not so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I would've liked a bit more of a mix-up with WoD mythology myself (and perhaps a bit more focus on going East, but that's because I'm Swedish. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). But I'm fine with this. It helps me see the era more clearly.<br /> <br /> Still, from how WoD has been presented before, religion has a big impact in the Astral, much less so in the Shadow. I don't see why it should've been different a thousand years ago.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857567#post857567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I did not read to it, but I do not see any Bale Hounds shout out that should be <i>natural</i> in Christian dominated Europe. Old World should be <i>crawling</i> with Malejin worshiping Uratha when confronted with Christianity and it's view on</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't help but to ask: Why?<br /> <br /> If anything I'd think Bale hounds would be on the rise after, when the concepts of Good and Evil were introduced to northern Europe, rather than the old view of Us and Them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857576#post857576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not want to choose one enemy amidst Church - I want to <i>deepen</i> mystery of fighting with other religion.<br /> <br /> In chapter, sacking monasteries and chapels do not seem much different than attacking the towns or castles - so it's &quot;favourless&quot;. Mention here and there vampires or Claimed seems more like random encounters than fighting alien religion temple. I was hoping for maybe at weird Bans or curses going on raiders? &quot;Alien&quot; christian spirts, not found in Scandinavia? Maybe not even some detailed stats, just mentioning that Christianity <i>was</i> a problem for Norse werewolves, as ALIEN religion itself, even when human Vikings embraced it easily? That Uratha in Europe had some weird fetishes and Gifts? Some things like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't a war between religions. It was raiding for wealth and power. Monasteries and churches weren't targeted because they were the focus of another religion, they were targeted because they had wealth.<br /> And Christianity wasn't too alien. It was easy for the Norse to pick up the idea that a mortal could've become a god. The hard part was never to make people believe in Jesus, the hard part was to make them stop believe in everything else.<br /> <br /> And why should it have been a problem? Why should Christian werewolves have other Gifts? People don't mystically turn into something else when they embrace a religion. Christians and Muslims are the same kind of people, why should there be any difference between Christians and the Norse?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857576#post857576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Great news - now how this relates to Uratha?</b> What does it gives me, as ST, to say to Viking Uratha and build story on this? 'You can attack your brothers in Christianity'? Well, what does this bring to my table?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why should it be any different than the wars between the Norse before Christianity came? Why should it be any different than the wars down on the continent? Why should it be any different from the wars on Ireland to set up the High King? Why should it be any different from the wars between the Byzantine Empire and the Lombards?<br /> <br /> The Norse were people too. There's nothing mysterious and otherworldly about belonging to another religion. [/QUOTE]<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T08:24:37-07:00","id":857716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857623#post857623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And why should it have been a problem? Why should Christian werewolves have other Gifts? People don't mystically turn into something else when they embrace a religion. Christians and Muslims are the same kind of people, why should there be any difference between Christians and the Norse?</div> </div> </div> </div>And more importantly, Christian, Muslim and Norse Uratha were the same kind of people. Individual belief may taint some things, but the Wolf Must Hunt trumps it all. The section did cover some of the ways belief in both religions might not jibe exactly with the 'proof' the werewolves face every day. But Christian, Muslim or Norse you're going to have the same Gifts and the same rites, though they may be practiced differently.<br /> <br /> As much as I'd like to have seen Bale Hounds, I think it's unfair to demand a fleshing out of something in a Dark Era when second edition has offered nothing more than an ambiguous sidebar about them. Stew has said he doesn't want to cover the Bale Hounds until he can do them justice. Once that happens, we can probably slot them in on our own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T09:21:21-07:00","id":857746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857623#post857623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, what do you mean &quot;How Shadow answer to coming of new religion?&quot;?. It's not like the Shadow of today is particularly shaped by religion, except around important religious centres. And even then it is THAT things are being believed in that causes a stir, not WHAT is being believed in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadow maybe not the belief itself ( there is not Jesus or Thor Spirit ) but <i>it follows</i> <i>emotions and decisions</i>. And those are very different in Vikings and Christian culture of that Era. For example, just see how pious Middle Ages Christians are and how they Heavenly Virtues are reflected in everyday life. I bet there are many 7 Virtuous spirits in Christdom, making important choir in Shadow. Vikings, on the other hand, are very feisty and power seeking. It <b>must</b> lead to different Shadow's ecologies at North and mainland Europe. Not too mention that Spirits would emulate angels and lesser gods in image at least in both cultures.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857623#post857623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, from how WoD has been presented before, religion has a big impact in the Astral, much less so in the Shadow. I don't see why it should've been different a thousand years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because we live now in very secular times - religion in modern Europe and USA has <b>much</b> lesser take on our lives than 1000 years ago, in Middle Ages. Shadow reflects actions and emotions - and those will be very different than those in modern days. So it shape diffrent spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857623#post857623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but to ask: Why?<br /> <br /> If anything I'd think Bale hounds would be on the rise after, when the concepts of Good and Evil were introduced to northern Europe, rather than the old view of Us and Them.</div> </div> </div> </div>In North - yes, Bale Hounds started to be later problem. Because North become Christian later on. Year ago I made whole topic <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460954-%E2%80%8Btheory-bale-hounds-as-effects-of-christianity\">why I think Bale Hounds are result of extensive Christanization</a> - and especial it's fight with \u201cpaganism\u201d. Check it out on details.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857623#post857623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wasn't a war between religions. It was raiding for wealth and power. Monasteries and churches weren't targeted because they were the focus of another religion, they were targeted because they had wealth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get this - but I think that this other religion lead to other Shadow in those places sacred by each culture. And this leads to have \u201calien guardians\u201d in those places. Different spirits. And so - different Numinas, and powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857623#post857623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Christianity wasn't too alien. It was easy for the Norse to pick up the idea that a mortal could've become a god. The hard part was never to make people believe in Jesus, the hard part was to make them stop believe in everything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is one of crucial things that different Norse and Christian Shadow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857623#post857623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And why should it have been a problem? Why should Christian werewolves have other Gifts?</div> </div> </div> </div>See my answers above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857623#post857623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People don't mystically turn into something else when they embrace a religion. Christians and Muslims are the same kind of people, why should there be any difference between Christians and the Norse?</div> </div> </div> </div>But it\u2019s culture clash. Norse and Christian werewolves are risen in different cultures - they <i>will</i> be different. We have Norse Uratha shown in chapter. We do not have shown Middle Ages Christian ones and their Shadow that our Vikings are sailing too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857623#post857623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Norse were people too. There's nothing mysterious and otherworldly about belonging to another religion.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right - but this religions has other implication in CoD universe and it\u2019s realms or monsters - and those will have <i>difference</i> on riding and war against them. So when question \u201cWhat is different between Norse and Christians as humans\u201d is \u201cNot very much\u201d. However answer on \u201cWhat are difference between Norse and Christian lands in CoD universe\u201d is \u201cA lot, they are different ecologies\u201d.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T09:33:55-07:00","id":857753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857623#post857623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but to ask: Why?<br /> <br /> If anything I'd think Bale hounds would be on the rise after, when the concepts of Good and Evil were introduced to northern Europe, rather than the old view of Us and Them.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it helps, it looks like Wyrd cut himself off; he was referring to something he's posted about on this forum before, how Christianity explicitly demonizes werewolves as agents of Satan and makes them all into the devil's agents on Earth. He has advocated that this would give Europe, especially during the medieval period, a disproportionately high population of Bale Hounds, as werewolves make their Change and have no real culture other than their own beliefs to fall back on, so they would presume they are &quot;supposed to be&quot; minions of evil, if I recall correctly.<br /> <br /> I think that the Shadows of the UK book for 1e actually mentions something about this... let me double-check...<br /> <br /> Yeah, in fact, all of Wyrd's commentary is actually based on established canon for UK werewolves, at least in 1e; page 24 of the Shadows of the UK sourcebook explains that the combination of a disproportionately high population of Ghost Wolves (that is, werewolves who change and can't be found by either the Pure or the Forsaken) and the fact that A: the dominant faith of the UK is Christianity, followed by Judaism and Islam, B: said religion literally demonizes werewolves as agents of Satan, C: true believers in the UK are extremely sincere due to the otherwise lack of importance of faith in daily life, means that said Ghost Wolves tend to turn to human religions to explain what has happened to them and form the conclusion that they are inherently and irredeemably evil as a result.<br /> <br /> What Wyrd is talking about is the fact that, during the time period, the Christian Church is a massively powerful influence on European society, to the point it's not entirely inaccurate to say that Europe is leaning towards theocracy. With the pagan faiths so violently stamped out, it's likely that, just as in the modern era, Europe has a disproportionately high population of Bale Hounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T09:49:15-07:00","id":857759,"title":"","content":"In a nutshell - everything that <b>VoidDrifter</b> wrote about Bale Hounds. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-02-2016, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T09:50:22-07:00","id":857760,"title":"","content":"That relies on Bale Hounds being the same as they were in first edition. It might be a valid stance to take if the Wolf and the Raven were in first edition, but it's not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T11:54:14-07:00","id":857836,"title":"","content":"There is inconsitency in <i>the Wolf and the Raven</i> Chapter. If this quote is true:<br /> <br /> <i>Despite their own knowledge of the Shadow and its deities, the Forsaken are none the wiser about the nature of the gods of Asgard. Some worship out of tradition or political convenience, regarding genuine faith as leaning towards the Flesh. <b>But almost all revere Mani, the moon god, as an embodiment of Luna.</b></i><br /> <br /> And this one:<br /> <br /> <i>Mani and his sister S\u00f3l are pursued through the skies by the vargr Hati and Sk\u00f6ll respectively, to be consumed during the same period.</i><br /> <br /> Should not this:<br /> <br /> <i>Most Forsaken identify Sk\u00f6ll as Winter Wolf, and see Helios\u2019 demise as a coherent if hubristic aspiration for that Firstborn. </i><br /> <br /> <b>Mention Helios as S\u00f3l in local Uratha mythology? </b><br /> <br /> And this Bone Shadows entry ficition:<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cSee? I told you the Christians were hiding something,\u201d bellowed Bjorn, knocking back wine from the altar he\u2019d just desecrated. Sven wasn\u2019t sure if he was talking about the silver at his feet or the corpse next to it. As the sun\u2019s rays reached the thing\u2019s blood, it began to boil and burn on the snow.<br /> \u201cI wonder what they did to anger Helios?\u201d<br /> \u201cI wonder where I can find more wine,\u201d Bjorn declared. As he kicked in the door of the next chapel, Sven stayed behind and prized the fangs from the corpse\u2019s maw. The Helions might take them as payment for the answer he sought.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Should change Helios and Helions into Sol and Solions (?) in text.</b><br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure that Vikings Uratha did not know Luna and Helios by they Latin names before christianization...<br /> <br /> And as we are at it - years before I <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths#post137256\">proposed the Vikings version of Lunes as Hjukis</a> - children stolen by Mani to become spirits servants. <b>I know this probably is too much for this chapter, but at least name like &quot;Maninus&quot; will be better than using latinized &quot;Lunes&quot;. &quot;Luna&quot; is unheard goddess for Vikings.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-02-2016, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T14:19:16-07:00","id":857918,"title":"","content":"The section you're quoting was one I actually cut down due to the word count, but I felt the transition from one set of names to the other was relatively coherent.<br /> <br /> And yes, I could've switched out Luna for Mani throughout the chapter, but I felt it would be confusing. Similarly, using <i>Amahan Iduth</i> throughout would've presented a barrier to more casual players or those who aren't overly familiar with First Tongue. With regard to in-character dialogue, I don't think it's too much of a stretch to use the names players are familiar with since I wasn't putting the rest of the dialogue in Danish or Swedish. I did consider including Hj\u00faki and Bil as sample Lunes but didn't have space, and felt that name-dropping them without a more thorough explanation would've fallen flat.<br /> <br /> As to the impact of religion on the Shadow, I don't think things would've differed majorly beyond aesthetics. Spirits of faith might have looked like angels and monks instead of the valkyries , but the Norse faith wasn't much more savage than Christianity because it was a savage time, and religion was pretty brutal all round. And the Norse were just as prone to public demonstrations of faith, such as blots and the public display of sacrificed animals. An underlying air of religion or faith might be present in more devout places, but when raiders show up that's probably going to be overpowered by one of fear and panic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10426-m-murray","name":"M.Murray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T22:32:52-07:00","id":858159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M.Murray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857918#post857918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The section you're quoting was one I actually cut down due to the word count, but I felt the transition from one set of names to the other was relatively coherent.</div> </div> </div> </div>By my sight they are not very coherent, when in one section you talk about Sol and in other about Helios. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Damn word count!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M.Murray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857918#post857918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, I could've switched out Luna for Mani throughout the chapter, but I felt it would be confusing. Similarly, using <i>Amahan Iduth</i> throughout would've presented a barrier to more casual players or those who aren't overly familiar with First Tongue.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing is to use actual Swedish and Danish in full text. Other is using localized names you mentioned few times before - without them, it seems like local Uratha use latinized names than their homeculture own. And by this I feel a bit betrayed when paying for Scandinavian Uratha setting. I got all hyped for seeing something exotic, other takes on gods, or Shadow. And in end I see it likes &quot;Sun is everywhere called Helios&quot;. It's bit disappointing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Confusing text is now - you state that they are called one way by North werewolves, then switch to latinized version they did not know befroe contact with Europs culture.<br /> <br /> Casualing game is bad take when you make specific historical setting - to play on it you go to play in Era, not make it &quot;werewolf barbarians&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M.Murray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857918#post857918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With regard to in-character dialogue, I don't think it's too much of a stretch to use the names players are familiar with since I wasn't putting the rest of the dialogue in Danish or Swedish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, why to try and localized things - we can all just call them Moon and Sun. Or better, &quot;Good Spirit&quot; and &quot;Jealous Spirit&quot; - Why to try conveying Norse setting we promised in Kickstarter? We can just play modern werewolf with totally globalized Uratha culture. Why to even try play true to the Vikings? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M.Murray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857918#post857918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to the impact of religion on the Shadow, I don't think things would've differed majorly beyond aesthetics. Spirits of faith might have looked like angels and monks instead of the valkyries , but the Norse faith wasn't much more savage than Christianity because it was a savage time, and religion was pretty brutal all round. And the Norse were just as prone to public demonstrations of faith, such as blots and the public display of sacrificed animals. An underlying air of religion or faith might be present in more devout places, but when raiders show up that's probably going to be overpowered by one of fear and panic.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no, no, no - you don't get me. When I wrote about religion, I do not mean the faith alone, rather wider culture of it. In Middle Ages Christanity is devoted to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seven_virtues\" target=\"_blank\">Seven Virtues</a> and, like <b>VoidDrifter</b> mention, Europe at that time is basically theocracy. The warriors and tradesmen leading Vikings, following their wandering gods, lead to completely different culture. That leads to different Essence creation, and that to diffrent spirits it's generate.<br /> <br /> Europeans generate most spirits of Faith ( in one god ), but also Chastity, Charity, Temperance and Humility, for example. In Viking society you will probably see more Faith ( in many gods ), but also Lust ( sex were much more open in their society ), Charity ( maybe? I do not know if Norse where famous from monetary help of others ), Boldness and Courage. It leads to different spirits, and by them, to different working Shadow.<br /> <br /> If monks in monasteries are following Temperance, Faith and Humility, Viking Uratha in early Raids Period could be totally dazed with other kinds of spirits - spirits that instead of fighting with them, can bind them or just totally quell them in to submission. Churches could be traps of unnatural silence for them, where Uratha must fight with environment itself. And bones and relics that Bone Shadows are taking with them to homeland can carry really nasty surprises...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-03-2016, 01:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T22:49:58-07:00","id":858170,"title":"","content":"Other smaller problems I have with chapter as written:<br /> <br /> <b>Where are <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berserker\" target=\"_blank\">\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</a>?</b> The &quot;wolf skins&quot;, wolf equivalent to berserkers. We have <i>\u00falfhethnar</i> in Blood Talons section, but I could not found is it the same as this much more recognized phrase.<br /> <br /> <b>Ergi connect only to the passive sex</b> - yes, it is a bit offensive for LGBT people. I understand the word count limits, but if you mention this in Bone Shadows section, you should point to broader implications of Ergi. To qutote by myself from other topic:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/360610-wod-dark-eras-was-ages-kickstarter-questions?p=855573#post855573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Paradim</b>, as minority that could be damaged by this subject I think there is better way to do it.<br /> <br /> Instead of:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Originally posted by <b>Actual Text</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Your character has been accused of being unmanly, or of passive homosexuality.</span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Originally posted by <b>Proposed Change</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Your character has been accused of unmanly behavior, such as showing cowardice.</span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <br /> I would go with that:<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Originally posted by <b>Proposed by WyrdHamster Change</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Your character has been accused of unmanly behavior, such as showing cowardice </span>or of passive homosexuality<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">.</span></i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">It's pointing that Ergi is more complex thing than liking anal sex and it's more general Norseman society thing. It lesser the point of &quot;only passive gays have Condition&quot; thing and should lesser slurps, with covering the fact that being passive <i>was</i> a problem for Vikings. If I would have known another example of Ergi trait, I would also mention it, to even more lesser the stigma and show broader problem. </span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T23:14:49-07:00","id":858180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=856025#post856025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm glad they updated the Gift of Technology because I needed that for a game set during the Crusades that I might be playing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I found this interesting, because when you get to Forsaken By Rome in the Dark Eras Companion, you'll see that we didn't update the Gift of Technology because (in my opinion) it didn't need it. <br /> <br /> What it does need is a note saying that the same Facets applied (and will continue to apply) to the technology of the age. In Roman (and Viking) times, this means things like fire, levers, edged weapons etc.<br /> <br /> The Gift of Technology as presented in WtF2 (and kudos to Chris for the great design work here) clearly demonstrates the Iron Masters were the adaptable, forward thinking tribe long before anyone considered such a thing might be needed. They designed their key Gift Facets around being timeless, and changing with the technology. They may have been less useful way back then, but the tribe was future-proofing.<br /> <br /> In my view, I also see that spirits of different times are able to impart Tech facets based on what the tech of the time is. This is possibly uniquely among the Gifts, and is another demonstration of why the Iron Masters are such a successful tribe.<br /> <br /> The most difficult part is separating natural phenomena from technology. For example, say you have two Uratha, one with Gift of Technology, the other with Gift of the Elementals. The technologist can extinguish the light, enhance the light, increase the heat of the forge, whatever - she's not targeting the fire in the forge, she's targeting the forge as a whole. What the fire does in response to that it its business.<br /> <br /> Whereas the werewolf with Elements targets the fire itself to make other things happen. He can control forest fires, light fires etc. whereas she can't, because those things aren't the tech.<br /> <br /> Or to put it another way, he says 'I want to improve the quality of my forged steel. I'll increase the fire in that forge, making it burn hotter so I can get more impurities out of the metal. Hope I don't overheat it and ruin the metal, or destroy the forge.' Roll dice and experiment with the conditions.<br /> <br /> She says 'I want to improve the quality of my steel. I control the Technology so the forge does whatever it needs, safely and within its limits, and my steel is so much better.'<br /> <br /> This was one reason why the Legions tended to have *vastly superior* equipment. <br /> <br /> (This takes nothing away from the replacement Gift in the Viking era, and groups will have access to both as their games require.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T00:20:35-07:00","id":858197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=858180#post858180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found this interesting, because when you get to Forsaken By Rome in the Dark Eras Companion, you'll see that we didn't update the Gift of Technology because (in my opinion) it didn't need it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find this interesting.<br /> <br /> I suppose Garble works like a mass Left-Handed Spanner from first edition in a more basic age, and the Wolf and Raven version of Shutdown, the extinguishing of lights, would be more applicable in Roman days than security cameras shutting off, obviously.<br /> <br /> The big change in the eras, for me because it's something my character has, was Iron Slave. In modern times you can use it to take over a 'mechanical vehicle' or other piece of engineering. For simplicity's sake lets say a car. You can possess a car, move it on its own. But can you make it run without gas, or electricity? I ask because Iron Slave was switched out during the Viking age, but you do sort of have an obvious vehicle Vikings might use that it may be useful to possess. A boat. I don't think it would count as a mechanical vehicle, but if you just narrowed it down to vehicle would you be able to move the boat if there was no wind? Because that would be very useful when it comes to getting out of doldrums. But if the Technology gift hasn't changed for Roman times, while you still have boats, you also have access to wagons. Obviously they exist in the time of Vikings but there's more of a clear emphasis on boats. Would a Slaved wagon be able to move on its own, or would the gift give power over the beasts used to move it?<br /> <br /> Feel I need to point out I do like the change in Iron Slave for the Viking period. I think it was a good example of an ability made through the lens of a hunter, and really useful for Vikings who could use it to track merchants or others. While I'm not sure about the themes of Forsaken by Rome odds are I would, personally, prefer to use Iron Minions as opposed to Iron Slave in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-03-2016, 03:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T00:59:39-07:00","id":858206,"title":"","content":"Re: Iron Slave - I apply the 'rule of cool' to this. It doesn't matter if the car has gas or not - the Uratha can make it go. How? If you actually need to answer that, it's powered by the trickle of Essence and the quickening of the spirit slumbering within the vehicle. An Uratha using Iron Slave on a rusted our husk of a car could still make it function and leave ignorant human observers baffled afterwards. Otherwise, how are you going to invoke the horror aspects after chasing the prey into a junkyard, where every headlight appears to be an eye, and the wrecks seem to glare malevolently at the prey?<br /> <br /> As for 'engineering' and 'mechanical vehicle', boats, chariots, wagons etc are all pieces of engineering. They're all mechanical. They have parts that do things. Even if the hull is largely an unmoving piece, they have sails and masts and tills and possibly oars. If anything, it would be more relevant to ask if modern cars and engineering count as mechanical, given how many of their functions are now controlled and operated by electronics.<br /> <br /> So, Uratha vikings in boats - yes, they can inhabit, steer and move their vessels in the absence of wind. Uratha-supported raiding parties are terrifying and outpace their human counterparts. They appear without warning on becalmed days when nothing should approach. They defy the storm that should keep them from the shore. They're terrifying hunters. Don't you agree this is as it should be?<br /> <br /> Same in Roman times. If the horse drawing the wagon goes lame or dies, the Uratha have another option. (Actually they have a few, but how many want to live down the taunts and jeers of their pack after pulling the wagon in Urshul form?) Even if the horse isn't lame, yes the Gift would give influence over the horse.<br /> <br /> They key here as I said above is to look at the whole as technology. Not the individual parts. The forge has fire and steel, but you don't view them as individual units - it's a forge. The Gift can't influence fire when it's just fire, but it can influence the forge. Similarly, the Gift can't influence fire when it's a forest fire, but Shutdown can dim the light of a campfire or the torches, because that's technology. The technology is important, and (repeating myself) it's a shining example of how forward-thinking and adaptable the Iron Masters were and are. There's a reason they're such a successful tribe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 04-03-2016, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T01:22:04-07:00","id":858219,"title":"","content":"One could say it's less about the letter of technology and more about...<br /> <br /> *sunglasses*<br /> <br /> the <i>spirit</i> of technology.<br /> <br /> *cough*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T02:21:15-07:00","id":858236,"title":"","content":"Arcee, I'm going to start calling you Nate. He tries to slip one of those into every game session we have <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T02:22:47-07:00","id":858238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=858206#post858206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Iron Slave - I apply the 'rule of cool' to this. It doesn't matter if the car has gas or not - the Uratha can make it go. How? If you actually need to answer that, it's powered by the trickle of Essence and the quickening of the spirit slumbering within the vehicle. An Uratha using Iron Slave on a rusted our husk of a car could still make it function and leave ignorant human observers baffled afterwards. Otherwise, how are you going to invoke the horror aspects after chasing the prey into a junkyard, where every headlight appears to be an eye, and the wrecks seem to glare malevolently at the prey?<br /> <br /> As for 'engineering' and 'mechanical vehicle', boats, chariots, wagons etc are all pieces of engineering. They're all mechanical. They have parts that do things. Even if the hull is largely an unmoving piece, they have sails and masts and tills and possibly oars. If anything, it would be more relevant to ask if modern cars and engineering count as mechanical, given how many of their functions are now controlled and operated by electronics.<br /> <br /> So, Uratha vikings in boats - yes, they can inhabit, steer and move their vessels in the absence of wind. Uratha-supported raiding parties are terrifying and outpace their human counterparts. They appear without warning on becalmed days when nothing should approach. They defy the storm that should keep them from the shore. They're terrifying hunters. Don't you agree this is as it should be?<br /> <br /> Same in Roman times. If the horse drawing the wagon goes lame or dies, the Uratha have another option. (Actually they have a few, but how many want to live down the taunts and jeers of their pack after pulling the wagon in Urshul form?) Even if the horse isn't lame, yes the Gift would give influence over the horse.<br /> <br /> They key here as I said above is to look at the whole as technology. Not the individual parts. The forge has fire and steel, but you don't view them as individual units - it's a forge. The Gift can't influence fire when it's just fire, but it can influence the forge. Similarly, the Gift can't influence fire when it's a forest fire, but Shutdown can dim the light of a campfire or the torches, because that's technology. The technology is important, and (repeating myself) it's a shining example of how forward-thinking and adaptable the Iron Masters were and are. There's a reason they're such a successful tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very well said. Rule of cool, or Essence, definitely seems to be the way to go about it. Though I have to admit the old horror trope of the car not starting is probably a lot scarier when you're inside the car. But I suppose it's something that could be replicated by other spirits of technology or supernaturals with powers that affect them.<br /> <br /> Good point about technology versus the individual parts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T08:01:08-07:00","id":858343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857746#post857746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shadow maybe not the belief itself ( there is not Jesus or Thor Spirit ) but <i>it follows</i> <i>emotions and decisions</i>. And those are very different in Vikings and Christian culture of that Era. For example, just see how pious Middle Ages Christians are and how they Heavenly Virtues are reflected in everyday life. I bet there are many 7 Virtuous spirits in Christdom, making important choir in Shadow. Vikings, on the other hand, are very feisty and power seeking. It <b>must</b> lead to different Shadow's ecologies at North and mainland Europe. Not too mention that Spirits would emulate angels and lesser gods in image at least in both cultures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly It follows the emotions. There will be spirits of Faith and Devotion on both sides. Why should the spirits care exactly what people have faith in? Why should they care what they are devoted to? It is - as you said - the emotion that matters.<br /> But even so, these spirits will be drowned out by the nature spirits. Spirits of disease, spirits of fear, war, hunger, anger, despair, joy, pride, and everything else that rises from human lives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857746#post857746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because we live now in very secular times - religion in modern Europe and USA has <b>much</b> lesser take on our lives than 1000 years ago, in Middle Ages. Shadow reflects actions and emotions - and those will be very different than those in modern days. So it shape diffrent spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. We also live in times when we don't have to spend winter fearing that there will be a late spring, and people will starve. Or late frost nights, and people will starve. Or drought, and people will starve. Or disease will strike, and people will die. Or that this happens to a neighbour, and in desperation, they try to take what is yours, and people will die.<br /> This is a vastly different setting, and I'm quite certain that religion is relatively low on the differences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857746#post857746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In North - yes, Bale Hounds started to be later problem. Because North become Christian later on. Year ago I made whole topic <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460954-%E2%80%8Btheory-bale-hounds-as-effects-of-christianity\">why I think Bale Hounds are result of extensive Christanization</a> - and especial it's fight with \u201cpaganism\u201d. Check it out on details.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves were never considered as anything other than monsters and/or foreigners in Scandinavia.<br /> Wolves were feared and hated, people who turned into wolves are monsters who deserve no mercy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857746#post857746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get this - but I think that this other religion lead to other Shadow in those places sacred by each culture. And this leads to have \u201calien guardians\u201d in those places. Different spirits. And so - different Numinas, and powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I simply can't agree here. They might take different appearances, but devotion is devotion, and faith is faith. The trappings change, but why should spirits care? It's the emotion behind it that brings in Essence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857746#post857746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this is one of crucial things that different Norse and Christian Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, you have to explain what you mean here, because I simply don't get it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857746#post857746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it\u2019s culture clash. Norse and Christian werewolves are risen in different cultures - they <i>will</i> be different. We have Norse Uratha shown in chapter. We do not have shown Middle Ages Christian ones and their Shadow that our Vikings are sailing too.</div> </div> </div> </div>The British Isles, which this chapter focuses on, isn't that different. The Irish and the Picts were both warrior cultures. And the Anglo-Saxons were close enough to the Norse, culturally speaking, that they could understand each other's languages. This was drifting by the time of the early Viking raids, as they were picking up the culture of the Romano-British.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=857746#post857746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are right - but this religions has other implication in CoD universe and it\u2019s realms or monsters - and those will have <i>difference</i> on riding and war against them. So when question \u201cWhat is different between Norse and Christians as humans\u201d is \u201cNot very much\u201d. However answer on \u201cWhat are difference between Norse and Christian lands in CoD universe\u201d is \u201cA lot, they are different ecologies\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they are. But unless a developer steps in on one side or the other, I think we'll be flinging opinion back and forth on each other on this point. (Again).<br /> <br /> But overall, I don't think there ever has been any indications that faith shapes the local shadow, anywhere in CofD. Shaping the astral? Sure! That's the place for thoughts. But the Shadow? I can't see I recall something like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=858170#post858170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other smaller problems I have with chapter as written:<br /> <br /> <b>Where are <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berserker\" target=\"_blank\">\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</a>?</b> The &quot;wolf skins&quot;, wolf equivalent to berserkers. We have <i>\u00falfhethnar</i> in Blood Talons section, but I could not found is it the same as this much more recognized phrase.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Wolf-hides would've been really great to have in the chapter as well.<br /> I also can't help but thinking that many Wolf-blooded cults would turn into Skinchangers, in order to emulate their Changed relatives and packmates.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=858170#post858170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ergi connect only to the passive sex</b> - yes, it is a bit offensive for LGBT people. I understand the word count limits, but if you mention this in Bone Shadows section, you should point to broader implications of Ergi. To qutote by myself from other topic:</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. It's offensive. But that's how the culture was back then. People change, culture change. The old Norse had very strong gender-roles, and for a man to take up female things was... discouraged. The side-bar is oversimplified, I admit, but it does get the point across.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T09:35:58-07:00","id":858372,"title":"","content":"Will omit &quot;faith an Christianity shape different Shadow thing&quot; - as you pointed, it will be only exchange of opinions until developers will go in to it.<br /> <br /> But on <i>Ergi</i> Condition I will discuss matter, as bisexual male in homosexual relationship from last five years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=858343#post858343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. It's offensive. But that's how the culture was back then. People change, culture change. The old Norse had very strong gender-roles, and for a man to take up female things was... discouraged. The side-bar is oversimplified, I admit, but it does get the point across.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it does not get point across. As was pointed by <b>Paradim </b>before - <i>Ergi</i> was not only passive homosexuality. Cowardliness is other example of <i>Ergi</i> behavior. There were others, if I remember my simple Google research on the topic. I think that Condition should show larger problem, not only targeting homophobia in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-03-2016, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T10:56:53-07:00","id":858402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=858372#post858372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will omit &quot;faith an Christianity shape different Shadow thing&quot; - as you pointed, it will be only exchange of opinions until developers will go in to it.<br /> <br /> But on <i>Ergi</i> Condition I will discuss matter, as bisexual male in homosexual relationship from last five years.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No, it does not get point across. As was pointed by <b>Paradim </b>before - <i>Ergi</i> was not only passive homosexuality. Cowardliness is other example of <i>Ergi</i> behavior. There were others, if I remember my simple Google research on the topic. I think that Condition should show larger problem, not only targeting homophobia in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Homosexual acts was, however, one of the main things called out for being unmanly. Other things are, such as cowardice and the practice of Seidh, but homosexuality the most common. Yes, the sidebar could've been a bit more sensitive, but it gets the point across. I don't see a problem here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T12:01:48-07:00","id":858429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=858236#post858236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arcee, I'm going to start calling you Nate. He tries to slip one of those into every game session we have <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Since the only Nate I know is the mastermind of the Leverage team, I fully accept this.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Seid has it right. Listen to him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-03-2016, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T12:22:09-07:00","id":858441,"title":"","content":"As to wording thing - Players are assumed to understand complex notions only by quick description of what <b>bl\u00f3t</b>, <b>seidr </b>or <b>vargr</b>, but remembering that <b>Mani</b> and <b>S\u00f3l</b> from the text are local names for Luna nad Helios is too much for casuals? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T12:34:39-07:00","id":858453,"title":"","content":"It explains what bl\u00f3t and seidr and vargr are.<br /> <br /> You've made your point and what you don't like and think should be changed, both here and elsewhere, are you just trying to harass now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T13:17:59-07:00","id":858475,"title":"","content":"The reason I emphasised the &quot;passive homosexuality&quot; bit was because it's directly related to Seidr; it's assumed that any practitioner has been the passive party in sex with a supernatural creature in exchange for these secrets, and while that is (in Viking culture) acceptable for women, it isn't for men. As a gay guy, I was conscious of the wording. Apparently I didn't choose the best phrasing, though I've shown it to a couple of people since the PDF release and they felt it was fine.<br /> <br /> Regarding the Tech Gift, I can see Bunyip's point, and that's definitely a cool way to interpret the Gift. I wanted to present the option, and it was alluded to in my brief. It's up to the players and the ST to decide which version to use. There was certainly a lot more in the way of machinery and mechanical industry in Rome. I was actually going to write a merchant lodge based on the concept of money as a tool but it took far more space to elaborate than I was comfortable giving it; Muspell worked better and seemed more appropriate with about half the words.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10426-m-murray","name":"M.Murray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T23:20:43-07:00","id":858790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M.Murray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=858475#post858475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason I emphasised the &quot;passive homosexuality&quot; bit was because it's directly related to Seidr; it's assumed that any practitioner has been the passive party in sex with a supernatural creature in exchange for these secrets, and while that is (in Viking culture) acceptable for women, it isn't for men. As a gay guy, I was conscious of the wording. Apparently I didn't choose the best phrasing, though I've shown it to a couple of people since the PDF release and they felt it was fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wording maybe is not the bad as on itself - but focusing <i>only</i> on homosexuality is, in my POV. Adding cowardliness and maybe other ( not sure is this there ) type of &quot;bad behavior&quot; to Ergi sources would mark this as more global Viking culture problem than strict homophobia. Also, much easier is to show hetero male players usage of <i>Ergi</i> when they characters are accused of being coward in battle than getting magical powers from the sex with other male, from my game experience.<br /> <br /> Not white-washing the problem - only showing wider range of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T08:07:34-07:00","id":859008,"title":"","content":"I was pleasantly surprised by this setting. I was not expecting too much but it turned out to be possibly my favorite out of all of Dark Eras. Here were some cool take away's that I got out of it.<br /> <br /> 1/ I like settings in Medieval cities and towns because they are small and densely populated by today's standards. In a modern city like Chicago it is possible for supernatural creatures to hide among the millions of people who live there, but in a medieval city of only a few thousand, in a much smaller area, the power brokers are literally only a few hundred meters from each other and cannot run so there is a sense of claustophobia. This was one of the reasons I was hoping for a &quot;Wild West&quot; setting but the viking settlements will do nicely. Having rival packs in a small town like Dublin or a viking settlement in Iceland makes the campaign more tense and personal. The Vampire Requiem Chroniclers book had a chapter devoted to Bottle Campaigns which I liked and can be applied here. In fact, there is the possibility that some scenes can be had on a viking boat when crossing the Atlantic. Imagine being at sea in the middle of nowhere and then realizing that some of the Rat hosts are on board...<br /> <br /> 2/ It was interesting to read that silver inlays were actually part of Viking blades. It makes sense that Vikings would display silver as a sign of wealth (medieval bling). In this case it is possible to wound a werewolf if the blade dug deep. I wonder how you could house rule this? Maybe that an exceptional success with a silver inlay blade would cause aggravated damage? How about if a blade wounds a werewolf every other (rounded down) wound is considered silver damage. <br /> <br /> 3/ Since we have Werewolves and Sin Eaters, it would be interesting to see a Viking hunter compact. Nothing would be more badass than a group of viking werewolves fighting a group of viking hunters. I could also imagine the practice of &quot;Silvering&quot; weapons in which a group of hunters go to the forge, melt an ingot of silver, and dip their blades into it before going to hunt wolves. Maybe a rule for that could be that the blade will cause the first ( or more) strike to cause silver damage after which the silver falls off. Anyways, it would make for epic storytelling<br /> <br /> 4/ Having adventures in the desolation of places like Greenland and Iceland would be pretty cool. I would imagine Storm Lords traveling to these places of extreme cold and desolation to hunt down claimed that have turned into dragons and giants (Beast crossover???). Using the cold weather as a possible asset and overcoming it. <br /> <br /> 5/ Other ideas could be to have the forsaken travel to lands with native populations (such as Greenland and Newfoundland), only to see the natives already have Pure overlords. This would be an excellent way to have werewolves waging war on each other using human proxies.<br /> <br /> Overall, it was a great chapter. Please make lots more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T12:24:08-07:00","id":859164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=858343#post858343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Werewolves were never considered as anything other than monsters and/or foreigners in Scandinavia.<br /> Wolves were feared and hated, people who turned into wolves are monsters who deserve no mercy.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually incorrect. If you are referring to the notion of the Varg nomenclature, they used to call outlaws wolves but they were not the werewolves. In fact I would argue the concept of werewolves in Icelandic and Viking age scandinavia would be considered more of a norm amongst the warrior culture. Case in point, Kveldulf from Egil's Saga.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ulf is said to have been a very clever farmer. he made a habit of getting up early to inspect what his farmhands or craftsmen were doing and to keep an eye on his cattle and cornfields. Sometimes he would talk to people who were in need of his advice, for he was shrewd and always to make useful suggestions. But every day towards evening he would grow so bad tempered that few people dared even address him. he always went to sleep early in the evening and woke up early in the morning. People claimed he was a shape-shifter and they called him Kveldulf (Evening wolf).&quot; Sagas of the Icelanders, from deluxe penguin classics page 9. <br /> <br /> The familiarity with which it is addressed leads me to believe it is considered a norm. Not only that, but the man was a local chieftain, and only left Norway after a rather nasty falling out with king Harald Fine hair. Another fine example might be king Harald himself using, in his own boat, only berserkers and Ulfhednar.<br /> <br /> More to the point, the entire 3rd chapter in 'Werewolf Histories' (a scholarly book compiled by a Danish anthropologist) discusses in great detail the animal warriors of norse society. <br /> <br /> Not to go complete scholar over here, but my proposed masters thesis is on the subject. I would argue that peoples dislike of Berserkers and their ilk stems not from a fear of shapeshifters in general but from behavioral issues. A masters of viking age history from university of Iceland (her name escapes me) did her thesis about these warriors suffering from ptsd. <br /> <br /> <br /> As far as the content of the chapter goes, I haven't read as much as i'd like, but from what I've seen its ok. Granted folk like me aren't the target audience, more from novices and gamers who do not understand or study the culture, and to that extent it is a fantastic addition. I was curious to see how they'd handle the whole worshipping fenris deal but it looks like the solution was simpler then I imagined, having come from the apocalypse fenrir tribe before. If anything the real issue I have is I believe it simply isn't large enough to cover all the material I want, and that isn't the fault of the author so much as the limitations imposed upon him. I imagine if they released a proper dark ages book for chronicles then things would be different, but as is I'm currently happy. Good job.<br /> <br /> As an addition to this, I see people arguing about how terrible x was vs y (ergi comes to mind). I would caution you from applying modern liberal thought patterns to a thousand year gone culture. It doesn't help anyone, beyond putting a bias one way or another as far as how one thinks a story should go. You wouldn't take an abraham lincoln style stance on freeing slaves if you lived in late 300's Rome would you? -fun fact to that, the slaves at the time were blonde haired blue eyed goths. Was considered fashionable to own a Tuetonic person.-","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T13:35:53-07:00","id":859227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-era-the-wolf-and-the-raven?p=859164#post859164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is actually incorrect. If you are referring to the notion of the Varg nomenclature, they used to call outlaws wolves but they were not the werewolves. In fact I would argue the concept of werewolves in Icelandic and Viking age scandinavia would be considered more of a norm amongst the warrior culture. Case in point, Kveldulf from Egil's Saga.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ulf is said to have been a very clever farmer. he made a habit of getting up early to inspect what his farmhands or craftsmen were doing and to keep an eye on his cattle and cornfields. Sometimes he would talk to people who were in need of his advice, for he was shrewd and always to make useful suggestions. But every day towards evening he would grow so bad tempered that few people dared even address him. he always went to sleep early in the evening and woke up early in the morning. People claimed he was a shape-shifter and they called him Kveldulf (Evening wolf).&quot; Sagas of the Icelanders, from deluxe penguin classics page 9.<br /> <br /> The familiarity with which it is addressed leads me to believe it is considered a norm. Not only that, but the man was a local chieftain, and only left Norway after a rather nasty falling out with king Harald Fine hair. Another fine example might be king Harald himself using, in his own boat, only berserkers and Ulfhednar.<br /> <br /> More to the point, the entire 3rd chapter in 'Werewolf Histories' (a scholarly book compiled by a Danish anthropologist) discusses in great detail the animal warriors of norse society.<br /> <br /> Not to go complete scholar over here, but my proposed masters thesis is on the subject. I would argue that peoples dislike of Berserkers and their ilk stems not from a fear of shapeshifters in general but from behavioral issues. A masters of viking age history from university of Iceland (her name escapes me) did her thesis about these warriors suffering from ptsd.<br /> <br /> <br /> As far as the content of the chapter goes, I haven't read as much as i'd like, but from what I've seen its ok. Granted folk like me aren't the target audience, more from novices and gamers who do not understand or study the culture, and to that extent it is a fantastic addition. I was curious to see how they'd handle the whole worshipping fenris deal but it looks like the solution was simpler then I imagined, having come from the apocalypse fenrir tribe before. If anything the real issue I have is I believe it simply isn't large enough to cover all the material I want, and that isn't the fault of the author so much as the limitations imposed upon him. I imagine if they released a proper dark ages book for chronicles then things would be different, but as is I'm currently happy. Good job.<br /> <br /> As an addition to this, I see people arguing about how terrible x was vs y (ergi comes to mind). I would caution you from applying modern liberal thought patterns to a thousand year gone culture. It doesn't help anyone, beyond putting a bias one way or another as far as how one thinks a story should go. You wouldn't take an abraham lincoln style stance on freeing slaves if you lived in late 300's Rome would you? -fun fact to that, the slaves at the time were blonde haired blue eyed goths. Was considered fashionable to own a Tuetonic person.-</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. So that happened later then? Apologies.<br /> In the area where I live (southern Sweden), being turned into a Werewolf was something that happened when you angered a witch (especially Finnish or Russian witches), and there are folk stories about entire villages going to flame out suspected werewolves.<br /> Then again, these woods have traditionally been very poor, and an attack by a pack of wolves (on the cattle, mind) could mean the death of families.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T16:18:31-07:00","id":859315,"title":"","content":"Really? That's odd to me as southern sweden was one of the last places to get fully christianized. Hell they ran the king of northern sweden out of the area for trying to impose christianity. I dont think they fully converted till the 1300's, though I may be mistaken on that.<br /> <br /> The folk stories about werewolf flame outs are likely from after the christianization, and likely the late middle ages, after the maellus malificorum came out. Though I'll admit I am not entirely familiar with the later history of Sweden as a whole. Though I'm sure everyone here would be curious to hear indigenous folk tales of werewolves, no matter what time period they originate from!<br /> <br /> Also goes with the first chapter in werewolf histories, which discusses how each culture has its own history for werewolves. There is no singular werewolf history, but rather a series of histories fully dependant on local folk tales. A differing example would be the latvian werewolves, which according to some of the accused, claimed to fight witches in the name of god with their beastily powers.<br /> <br /> Edit: as an aside, the Danes apparently believed that stretching horse placenta across 4 posts and climbing through it made child birth painless, but your son would be a werewolf. A daughter would be a nightmare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":1939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","user":"Lyrics Of War","date":". 04-04-2016, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T21:58:06-07:00","id":859464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M.Murray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855762-dark-